 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Crystal begins depositing $450 per month from her paycheck each month in her employer-based 401(k) account. The employer matches $350 of each deposit. Crystal expects the return to average 9% per year, compounded annually.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519717,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How much will Crystal’s account be worth if she keeps making those payments for 25 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$813,128.60"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The future value of an ordinary annuity or mutual fund is <span data-math=\"FV = pmt \\times \\frac{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}{{\\frac{r}{n}}}\"></span>, where <i>FV</i> is the future value of the annuity, <i>pmt</i> is the payment, <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. It is important to note that the number of deposits per year and the number of compounding periods per year must be the same.</p>\n<p>It will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 1 \\right) \\times \\left( {25} \\right) = 25\"></span></p>\n<p>The combined monthly payment is <span data-math=\"{\\text{450  +  350  =  \\$800}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>It is only compounded annually, so for the payment, multiply the monthly payment by 12.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{12(800)  =  \\$9,600}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"FV = 9,600 \\times \\frac{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.09}}{1}} \\right)}^{25}} - 1} \\right)}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{0.09}}{1}} \\right)}}{\\text{  =  \\$813,128}}{\\text{.60}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The extra parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n<p>Crystal’s account will be worth $813,128.60.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 519718,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What will her account be worth without the matching funds?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$457,384.83"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>It is only compounded annually, so for the payment, multiply the monthly payment by 12.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{12(450)  =  \\$5,400}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"FV = 5,400 \\times \\frac{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.09}}{1}} \\right)}^{25}} - 1} \\right)}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{0.09}}{1}} \\right)}}{\\text{  =  \\$457,384}}{\\text{.84}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Without matching funds, her account will be worth $457,384.84.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
